// CF-2: `||` in a guard is a SATURATING ADD of the two 0/1 comparisons.
// As with `&&` it is the last link that carries the cc_update, at fx12,
// and the comparisons themselves stay fp32 in half-register lanes.
//
// (Our general path lowers `||` as MAX, which is equal on 0/1 and
// byte-divergent from the reference's saturating add.  That divergence
// predates CF-2 and moves rows that have nothing to do with discard, so
// it is its own item; this fixture asserts the CHAIN - two comparisons,
// one combiner carrying the cc_update, one KIL - not the opcode.)
void main(float4 c : TEXCOORD0, out float4 o : COLOR)
{
    if (c.a < 0.1 || c.r > 0.9) discard;
    o = c;
}
